</section>
<section id="S2.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsection">2.5  Multi-Signal Score Fusion</h3>

<div id="S2.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">CombSUM, CombMNZ <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>]</cite>, and Reciprocal Rank
Fusion <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>]</cite> combine ranked lists from multiple retrieval
systems for rank aggregation.
ScoreGate instead fuses two continuous scores from a single candidate set
to make a <em id="S2.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">binary</em> keep/discard decision—a fundamentally different
application of score fusion.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_section" style="font-size:120%;">3  Problem Formulation</h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> denote a user query.
A two-stage RAG pipeline produces a candidate set
<math id="S3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C=\{c_{1},\ldots,c_{N}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C=\{c_{1},\ldots,c_{N}\}</annotation></semantics></math> of the top-<math id="S3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> chunks ranked by the
cross-encoder reranker.
Each chunk <math id="S3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is associated with a score pair:</p>
<table id="S3.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}=(s_{i},\ r_{i})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}=(s_{i},\ r_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> is the bi-encoder cosine similarity between the
<math id="S3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-normalised query and chunk embeddings, and <math id="S3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> is the
cross-encoder relevance score normalised to <math id="S3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> by min–max scaling
over <math id="S3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>.
Per-query min–max normalisation is intentional: the thresholds
<math id="S3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> are derived from the same normalised distributions,
so they are internally consistent.
More importantly, the relative ordering of chunks within a query is
preserved under any monotone transformation.
A chunk classified as B3 (<math id="S3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}\geq\tau_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}\geq\tau_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>) is affirmed by the
cross-encoder <em id="S3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">relative to the other candidates for that query</em>—
the signal we want: whether the reranker considers this chunk relevant
given the competition, not whether it exceeds an absolute threshold.
The false-positive rate of 5% used to derive <math id="S3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> (Section 4.1)
was computed on the same per-query normalised scores, so the 5% FPR
claim is consistent with this normalisation.
Table <a href="#S3.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 3 Problem Formulation ‣ ScoreGate: Adaptive Chunk Selection forRetrieval-Augmented Generationvia Dual-Score Statistical Fusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> confirms empirically that per-query min–max
scaling outperforms raw logits and sigmoid normalisation on both
ARB recall and MS MARCO MRR@10.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span>
<span id="S3.T2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Reranker score normalisation ablation.</span>
Per-query min–max scaling outperforms alternatives by
producing the strongest B3/B4 score separation.
Results on ARB (Sem. Relevant recall) and MS MARCO
(200-query dev set, MRR@10).
</figcaption>
<table id="S3.T2.4" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S3.T2.4.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S3.T2.4.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="S3.T2.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Normalisation</span></th>
<th id="S3.T2.4.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S3.T2.4.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Recall (Sem. Rel.)</span></th>
<th id="S3.T2.4.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S3.T2.4.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">MRR@10</span></th>
<th id="S3.T2.4.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S3.T2.4.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Avg. <math id="S3.T2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|C^{\prime}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|C^{\prime}|</annotation></semantics></math></span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S3.T2.4.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S3.T2.4.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">Raw logits</th>
<td id="S3.T2.4.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">96.8%</td>
<td id="S3.T2.4.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">0.392</td>
<td id="S3.T2.4.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">7.1</td></tr>
<tr id="S3.T2.4.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S3.T2.4.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Sigmoid</th>
<td id="S3.T2.4.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">97.5%</td>
<td id="S3.T2.4.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.395</td>
<td id="S3.T2.4.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">6.8</td></tr>
<tr id="S3.T2.4.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S3.T2.4.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb"><span id="S3.T2.4.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Min–max (ours)</span></th>
<td id="S3.T2.4.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="S3.T2.4.4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">99.34%</span></td>
<td id="S3.T2.4.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="S3.T2.4.4.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.401</span></td>
<td id="S3.T2.4.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="S3.T2.4.4.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">6.1</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="S3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Per-query min–max normalisation produced the strongest separation
between B3 and B4 regions, likely because it preserves within-query
score ranking while adapting to query-specific reranker score
distributions.
The standard pipeline selects
<math id="S3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\prime}=\{c_{(1)},\ldots,c_{(K)}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\prime}=\{c_{(1)},\ldots,c_{(K)}\}</annotation></semantics></math> by fixed truncation at rank <math id="S3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>.
We seek instead an adaptive selection function <math id="S3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> such that:</p>
<table id="S3.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(C)\rightarrow C^{\prime}\subseteq C,\quad 1\leq|C^{\prime}|\leq K_{\max}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⊆</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(C)\rightarrow C^{\prime}\subseteq C,\quad 1\leq|C^{\prime}|\leq K_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> requires no model inference beyond the reranker call already
performed, and <math id="S3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|C^{\prime}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|C^{\prime}|</annotation></semantics></math> is determined by the score distribution of <math id="S3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>
rather than fixed a priori.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_section" style="font-size:120%;">4  ScoreGate Method</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#S4.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ 4 ScoreGate Method ‣ ScoreGate: Adaptive Chunk Selection forRetrieval-Augmented Generationvia Dual-Score Statistical Fusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> illustrates the complete ScoreGate pipeline.
We use the term <em id="S4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">adaptive cardinality</em> rather than <em id="S4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">filtering</em>
to emphasise that ScoreGate does not re-rank or post-process a
fixed-size set—it determines the <em id="S4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">size</em> of the set passed to
the generator, which can be anywhere from 0 to MAX-<math id="S4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> depending on
the query’s score distribution.
The distinction matters: a filter operates on a fixed-<math id="S4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> input;
ScoreGate replaces the fixed-<math id="S4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> decision itself.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.F1" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2606.14269v1/fig_pipeline.png" id="S4.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/328;" width="476" height="328" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 1: </span>
<span id="S4.F1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">The ScoreGate pipeline.</span>
A user query triggers bi-encoder vector retrieval of top-<math id="S4.F1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> candidates,
followed by cross-encoder reranking to obtain score pairs <math id="S4.F1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s_{i},r_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s_{i},r_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Data-driven thresholds (<math id="S4.F1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{s}\!=\!0.70" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>0.70</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{s}\!=\!0.70</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.F1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{r}\!=\!0.08" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>0.08</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{r}\!=\!0.08</annotation></semantics></math>) partition
each chunk into one of four buckets (B1–B4).
B1 and B3 are retained unconditionally; B4 is discarded
unconditionally; B2 candidates are retained only if the fusion score
<math id="S4.F1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}\geq 0.255" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0.255</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}\geq 0.255</annotation></semantics></math>.
The filtered set <math id="S4.F1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded above by MAX-<math id="S4.F1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> and passed to
the generator.
</figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsection">4.1  Score Threshold Derivation</h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We obtain thresholds <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> from query log statistics.
<math id="S4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> is the median bi-encoder cosine similarity over the top-<math id="S4.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>
candidate set aggregated across a representative query sample (<math id="S4.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\!=\!40" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>40</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\!=\!40</annotation></semantics></math>).
<math id="S4.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> is the reranker score corresponding to a false-positive rate of
approximately 5% on a held-out relevance-annotated validation set.
From our production logs:</p>
<table id="S4.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{s}=0.70\qquad\tau_{r}=0.08" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.70</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.08</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{s}=0.70\qquad\tau_{r}=0.08</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Both thresholds are computed once from log data and applied at inference
time without per-query recalculation.
The threshold derivation procedure is domain-agnostic: re-running the
median-similarity and 5%-FPR calibration on a domain-specific query
sample produces new <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> values without any model
retraining. Whether the four-bucket structure and fusion weight
<math id="S4.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\!=\!0.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>0.3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\!=\!0.3</annotation></semantics></math> generalise across domains is an empirical question
this is evaluated empirically in Section 4.3 (Figure <a href="#S4.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ 4.3 Weighted Fusion Score and Asymmetric Thresholds ‣ 4 ScoreGate Method ‣ ScoreGate: Adaptive Chunk Selection forRetrieval-Augmented Generationvia Dual-Score Statistical Fusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Score distributions by relevance category.</h4>

<div id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#S4.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ Score distributions by relevance category. ‣ 4.1 Score Threshold Derivation ‣ 4 ScoreGate Method ‣ ScoreGate: Adaptive Chunk Selection forRetrieval-Augmented Generationvia Dual-Score Statistical Fusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> shows empirical score distributions
for <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> across the three ARB relevance categories.
Irrelevant chunks cluster at low <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and low <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>; Relevant
chunks at high <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and high <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Semantically Relevant chunks span a wide <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> range but maintain
elevated <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>—confirming the B3 pattern that motivates
ScoreGate’s asymmetric thresholds.
The right panel shows the distribution of retained chunk counts
<math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|C^{\prime}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|C^{\prime}|</annotation></semantics></math> across ARB queries, confirming adaptive behaviour: most
queries retain 2–5 chunks rather than a fixed <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\!=\!10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\!=\!10</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.F2" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2606.14269v1/fig_distributions.png" id="S4.F2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/133;" width="476" height="133" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 2: </span>
<span id="S4.F2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Left/Centre:</span> Score distributions by relevance category
on the ARB. Dashed lines mark <math id="S4.F2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{s}\!=\!0.70" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>0.70</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{s}\!=\!0.70</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S4.F2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{r}\!=\!0.08" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>0.08</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{r}\!=\!0.08</annotation></semantics></math>. Semantically Relevant chunks (blue) have
elevated <math id="S4.F2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> despite low <math id="S4.F2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>—the B3 pattern.
<span id="S4.F2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Right:</span> Distribution of retained chunks per query
(<math id="S4.F2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|C^{\prime}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|C^{\prime}|</annotation></semantics></math>) on the ARB, demonstrating adaptive cardinality
(mean 4.4 vs fixed <math id="S4.F2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\!=\!10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\!=\!10</annotation></semantics></math>).
</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsection">4.2  Four-Region Score Partition</h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The thresholds <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> partition the unit square
<math id="S4.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]{\times}[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]{\times}[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> of score pairs into four axis-aligned,
non-overlapping regions.
Each candidate <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s_{i},r_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s_{i},r_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> falls into exactly one bucket, as shown in
Figure <a href="#S4.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ 4.2 Four-Region Score Partition ‣ 4 ScoreGate Method ‣ ScoreGate: Adaptive Chunk Selection forRetrieval-Augmented Generationvia Dual-Score Statistical Fusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> and Table <a href="#S4.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 4.2 Four-Region Score Partition ‣ 4 ScoreGate Method ‣ ScoreGate: Adaptive Chunk Selection forRetrieval-Augmented Generationvia Dual-Score Statistical Fusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.F3" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2606.14269v1/fig2_quadrant.png" id="S4.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:295/249;" width="295" height="249" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 3: </span>
<span id="S4.F3.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Four-region partition of the <math id="S4.F3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s_{i},r_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s_{i},r_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> score space.</span>
Vertical dashed line at <math id="S4.F3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{s}\!=\!0.70" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>0.70</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{s}\!=\!0.70</annotation></semantics></math>;
horizontal dashed line at <math id="S4.F3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{r}\!=\!0.08" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>0.08</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{r}\!=\!0.08</annotation></semantics></math>.
<span id="S4.F3.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">B1</span> (green, top-right): both scores affirm relevance—keep
unconditionally.
<span id="S4.F3.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">B2</span> (orange, bottom-right): high similarity, low
relevance—apply fusion threshold <math id="S4.F3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}\geq 0.255" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0.255</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}\geq 0.255</annotation></semantics></math>.
<span id="S4.F3.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">B3</span> (blue, top-left): low similarity, high relevance
(vocabulary mismatch)—apply lower threshold <math id="S4.F3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}\geq 0.15" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0.15</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}\geq 0.15</annotation></semantics></math>.
<span id="S4.F3.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">B4</span> (red, bottom-left): both scores reject—discard
unconditionally.
Data points are representative examples from the Annotated
Relevance Benchmark (ARB).
</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S4.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 3: </span>
<span id="S4.T3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Four-region score-space partition and retention rules.</span>
The B3 threshold is intentionally lower than B2 because the
cross-encoder has already affirmed relevance in B3; the only
disconfirming signal is lexical distance, which we treat as
less informative than cross-encoder affirmation.
</figcaption>
<table id="S4.T3.4" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S4.T3.4.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T3.4.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T3.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Region</span></th>
<th id="S4.T3.4.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><math id="S4.T3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.T3.4.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> condition</span></th>
<th id="S4.T3.4.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><math id="S4.T3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.T3.4.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> condition</span></th>
<th id="S4.T3.4.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T3.4.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Retention rule</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S4.T3.4.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T3.4.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">B1</td>
<td id="S4.T3.4.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><math id="S4.T3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq\tau_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq\tau_{s}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S4.T3.4.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><math id="S4.T3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq\tau_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq\tau_{r}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S4.T3.4.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">Always keep</td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T3.4.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T3.4.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">B2</td>
<td id="S4.T3.4.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="S4.T3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq\tau_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq\tau_{s}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S4.T3.4.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="S4.T3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;\tau_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;\tau_{r}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S4.T3.4.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Keep if <math id="S4.T3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}\geq 0.255" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0.255</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}\geq 0.255</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T3.4.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T3.4.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">B3</td>
<td id="S4.T3.4.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="S4.T3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;\tau_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;\tau_{s}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S4.T3.4.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="S4.T3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq\tau_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq\tau_{r}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S4.T3.4.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Keep if <math id="S4.T3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}\geq 0.15" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0.15</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}\geq 0.15</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T3.4.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T3.4.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">B4</td>
<td id="S4.T3.4.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb"><math id="S4.T3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;\tau_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;\tau_{s}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S4.T3.4.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb"><math id="S4.T3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;\tau_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;\tau_{r}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S4.T3.4.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">Always discard</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsection">4.3  Weighted Fusion Score and Asymmetric Thresholds</h3>

<div id="S4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For candidates in B2 and B3, a deterministic rule based on a single score
is unreliable because the two scores carry conflicting evidence.
We compute a weighted linear fusion score:</p>
<table id="S4.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}=\alpha\cdot s_{i}+(1-\alpha)\cdot r_{i},\qquad\alpha=0.3" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}=\alpha\cdot s_{i}+(1-\alpha)\cdot r_{i},\qquad\alpha=0.3</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The weight <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\!=\!0.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>0.3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\!=\!0.3</annotation></semantics></math> assigns 70% of the fusion weight to <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>
and 30% to <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.
This asymmetry is justified by two properties of cross-encoder rerankers:
(1) cross-encoders are trained directly on human relevance judgements via
supervised contrastive learning over query–document pairs, producing scores
better calibrated to human relevance than cosine similarity in the
bi-encoder embedding space;
(2) cross-encoder scores are conditioned on the specific query, whereas
bi-encoder similarity measures proximity in a shared space optimised for
retrieval recall rather than precision.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The retention thresholds <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{B2}\!=\!0.255" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>0.255</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{B2}\!=\!0.255</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S4.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{B3}\!=\!0.15" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>0.15</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{B3}\!=\!0.15</annotation></semantics></math> are asymmetric by design.
In B2, the cross-encoder has rejected the chunk (<math id="S4.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}&lt;\tau_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}&lt;\tau_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>), so a
higher fusion score is required to override that rejection.
In B3, the cross-encoder has affirmed the chunk (<math id="S4.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}\geq\tau_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}\geq\tau_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>), and
the only disconfirming signal is low bi-encoder similarity—a “lexical
gap” we treat as less informative than cross-encoder affirmation.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#S4.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ 4.3 Weighted Fusion Score and Asymmetric Thresholds ‣ 4 ScoreGate Method ‣ ScoreGate: Adaptive Chunk Selection forRetrieval-Augmented Generationvia Dual-Score Statistical Fusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> shows <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> sensitivity to <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>
across seven values; the surface peaks at <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\!=\!0.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>0.3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\!=\!0.3</annotation></semantics></math> and
declines monotonically.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.F4" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2606.14269v1/fig_alpha.png" id="S4.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:390/249;" width="390" height="249" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 4: </span>
<span id="S4.F4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Fusion weight sensitivity (ARB, Semantically Relevant).</span>
<math id="S4.F4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> peaks at <math id="S4.F4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\!=\!0.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>0.3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\!=\!0.3</annotation></semantics></math> and declines monotonically in both
directions, confirming that reranker-dominant weighting (70% to
<math id="S4.F4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, 30% to <math id="S4.F4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>) is empirically necessary.
The unimodal shape indicates the optimum is stable under evaluated conditions: performance
degrades gracefully rather than catastrophically away from
<math id="S4.F4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\!=\!0.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>0.3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\!=\!0.3</annotation></semantics></math>.
</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsection">4.4  Cardinality Bound</h3>

<div id="S4.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">After applying the four-region rules, the retained set <math id="S4.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded by:</p>
<table id="S4.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|C^{\prime}|\leftarrow\min(|C^{\prime}|,\ K_{\max})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|C^{\prime}|\leftarrow\min(|C^{\prime}|,\ K_{\max})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">When the ceiling is binding (<math id="S4.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|C^{\prime}|&gt;K_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|C^{\prime}|&gt;K_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>), we retain the <math id="S4.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>
chunks with the highest fusion scores <math id="S4.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.
This ranking is empirically motivated: <math id="S4.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the same weighted combination
of both relevance signals used throughout ScoreGate, so the dropped
chunks are precisely those with the weakest combined evidence for
relevance among an already-filtered set.
In our deployment <math id="S4.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\max}\!=\!10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\max}\!=\!10</annotation></semantics></math>.
The ceiling was binding in 14 of the 300 ARB queries (4.7%),
resulting in 31 dropped chunks.
Of these, 23 were Irrelevant (correctly dropped), 4 were Relevant,
and 4 were Semantically Relevant (8 total false negatives introduced
by the ceiling).
By bucket, dropped chunks were: B2 = 4, B3 = 9, B4 = 18
(no B1 chunks were dropped).
The 9 dropped B3 chunks are the most operationally significant:
these are vocabulary-mismatch chunks affirmed by the reranker but
with lower <math id="S4.SS4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> than other retained chunks due to their low <math id="S4.SS4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.
This confirms the vocabulary-mismatch edge case described in Section 4.1 and motivates
raising MAX-<math id="S4.SS4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> in knowledge-intensive deployment contexts.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsection">4.5  Algorithm</h3>

<div id="S4.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The complete ScoreGate procedure is summarised in
Algorithm 1.
Time complexity is <math id="S4.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(N\log N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(N\log N)</annotation></semantics></math> dominated by the final sort.
With <math id="S4.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\!=\!40" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>40</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\!=\!40</annotation></semantics></math>, this contributes negligible overhead relative to
cross-encoder inference.</p>
</div>
<figure id="algorithm1" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="algorithm1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span>ScoreGate</figcaption>
<div id="algorithm1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="algorithm1.4.1" class="ltx_listingline">
<span id="algorithm1.4.1.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="algorithm1.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> </span><math id="algorithm1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C=\{(s_{i},r_{i})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C=\{(s_{i},r_{i})\}</annotation></semantics></math>, thresholds <math id="algorithm1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{s},\tau_{r},\theta_{B2},\theta_{B3}\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{s},\tau_{r},\theta_{B2},\theta_{B3}\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>,
weight <math id="algorithm1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, MAX-<math id="algorithm1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.2" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.2.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="algorithm1.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span> </span><math id="algorithm1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\prime}\subseteq C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⊆</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\prime}\subseteq C</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="algorithm1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|C^{\prime}|\leq\text{MAX-}K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mtext>MAX-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|C^{\prime}|\leq\text{MAX-}K</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1</span></span>
            <math id="algorithm1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\prime}\leftarrow\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\prime}\leftarrow\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">2</span></span>
            <span id="algorithm1.4.4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">foreach</span> <em id="algorithm1.4.4.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s_{i},r_{i})\in C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s_{i},r_{i})\in C</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm1.4.4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.5" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">3</span></span>
            <math id="algorithm1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}\leftarrow\alpha\cdot s_{i}+(1-\alpha)\cdot r_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}\leftarrow\alpha\cdot s_{i}+(1-\alpha)\cdot r_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.6" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">4</span></span>
            <span id="algorithm1.4.6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <em id="algorithm1.4.6.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}\geq\tau_{s}\;\wedge\;r_{i}\geq\tau_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.502em">∧</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}\geq\tau_{s}\;\wedge\;r_{i}\geq\tau_{r}</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm1.4.6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.7" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">5</span></span>
            <math id="algorithm1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\prime}\leftarrow C^{\prime}\cup\{i\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\prime}\leftarrow C^{\prime}\cup\{i\}</annotation></semantics></math>   <span id="algorithm1.4.7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="algorithm1.4.7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">B1: always keep</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.8" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">6</span></span>
            <span id="algorithm1.4.8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else if</span> <em id="algorithm1.4.8.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}\geq\tau_{s}\;\wedge\;r_{i}&lt;\tau_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.502em">∧</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}\geq\tau_{s}\;\wedge\;r_{i}&lt;\tau_{r}</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm1.4.8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.9" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">7</span></span>
            <span id="algorithm1.4.9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <em id="algorithm1.4.9.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}\geq\theta_{B2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}\geq\theta_{B2}</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm1.4.9.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span> <math id="algorithm1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\prime}\leftarrow C^{\prime}\cup\{i\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\prime}\leftarrow C^{\prime}\cup\{i\}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.10" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>   <span id="algorithm1.4.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="algorithm1.4.10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">B2: high bar</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.11" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">8</span></span>
            <span id="algorithm1.4.11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else if</span> <em id="algorithm1.4.11.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}&lt;\tau_{s}\;\wedge\;r_{i}\geq\tau_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.502em">∧</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}&lt;\tau_{s}\;\wedge\;r_{i}\geq\tau_{r}</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm1.4.11.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.12" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.12.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">9</span></span>
            <span id="algorithm1.4.12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <em id="algorithm1.4.12.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}\geq\theta_{B3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}\geq\theta_{B3}</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm1.4.12.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span> <math id="algorithm1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\prime}\leftarrow C^{\prime}\cup\{i\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\prime}\leftarrow C^{\prime}\cup\{i\}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.13" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>   <span id="algorithm1.4.13.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="algorithm1.4.13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">B3: low bar (vocab mismatch)</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.14" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.14.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">10</span></span>
            <span id="algorithm1.4.14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else</span> skip   <span id="algorithm1.4.14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="algorithm1.4.14.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">B4: always discard</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.15" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.15.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">11</span></span>
            <span id="algorithm1.4.15.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> top-MAX-<math id="algorithm1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="algorithm1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> ranked by <math id="algorithm1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> descending
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.16" class="ltx_listingline">
</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_section" style="font-size:120%;">5  Experiments</h2>

<section id="S5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsection">5.1  Datasets and Setup</h3>

<div id="S5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate ScoreGate on three datasets spanning public benchmarks
and internal deployment data, ordered from most to least reproducible.</p>
</div>
<section id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">MS MARCO Passage Ranking (primary benchmark).</h4>

<div id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">MS MARCO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite> is a large-scale public passage retrieval
benchmark with 8.8M passages and official relevance judgements
(qrels).
We randomly sample 200 queries from the official dev set for
evaluation.
MS MARCO provides the primary reproducible evidence for ScoreGate’s
generalisation, as both the corpus and qrels are publicly available
and the evaluation protocol is standard.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Annotated Relevance Benchmark (ARB) — internal validation.</h4>

<div id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To validate ScoreGate’s behaviour in the specific production
deployment context, we constructed 300 (query, chunk, relevance
label) triples from the internal knowledge base (approximately
12,000 chunks, average length 180 tokens, split at paragraph
boundaries with 20-token overlap).
Queries were sampled uniformly at random from the production query
log (excluding the 200-query threshold-tuning window) and stratified
post-hoc into three equal categories of 100 triples each:
<em id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Irrelevant</em>, <em id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Relevant</em>, and <em id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Semantically Relevant</em>.
We note that the ARB knowledge base is shared with the corpus used
to derive <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{B2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{B2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and
<math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{B3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{B3}</annotation></semantics></math>; queries are drawn from a disjoint time window
but corpus-level statistics may overlap.
The ARB is therefore best interpreted as deployment validation
rather than an independent generalisation test.
The 100/100/100 balanced split is a deliberate diagnostic design;
Table <a href="#S5.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ Annotated Relevance Benchmark (ARB) — internal validation. ‣ 5.1 Datasets and Setup ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ ScoreGate: Adaptive Chunk Selection forRetrieval-Augmented Generationvia Dual-Score Statistical Fusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> contrasts this with observed production
distribution.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span>
<span id="S5.T4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Category distribution: ARB vs. production (RWD).</span>
The ARB uses a balanced design for diagnostic control;
real production traffic is dominated by irrelevant candidates.
</figcaption>
<table id="S5.T4.4" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S5.T4.4.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S5.T4.4.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="S5.T4.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Dataset</span></th>
<th id="S5.T4.4.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S5.T4.4.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Irrelevant</span></th>
<th id="S5.T4.4.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S5.T4.4.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Relevant</span></th>
<th id="S5.T4.4.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S5.T4.4.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sem. Relevant</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S5.T4.4.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S5.T4.4.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">ARB (diagnostic)</th>
<td id="S5.T4.4.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">33%</td>
<td id="S5.T4.4.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">33%</td>
<td id="S5.T4.4.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">33%</td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T4.4.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S5.T4.4.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb">RWD (production)</th>
<td id="S5.T4.4.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">71%</td>
<td id="S5.T4.4.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">18%</td>
<td id="S5.T4.4.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">11%</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Annotators were blind to model scores <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s_{i},r_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s_{i},r_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> during labelling.
Labels were assigned by three domain-expert annotators with disagreements
resolved by majority vote (inter-annotator agreement <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\kappa}\!=\!0.87" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>0.87</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\kappa}\!=\!0.87</annotation></semantics></math>
by Fleiss’ <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> for three raters <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>; per-category
<math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>: Irrelevant 0.91, Relevant 0.88, Semantically Relevant 0.82).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Candidate Set Size Sensitivity.</h4>

<div id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We additionally evaluated retrieval candidate set sizes
<math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\in\{20,40,60\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>40</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>60</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\in\{20,40,60\}</annotation></semantics></math> on the ARB.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T5" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5: </span>
<span id="S5.T5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Effect of candidate set size <math id="S5.T5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> on ScoreGate performance.</span>
Recall improves measurably from <math id="S5.T5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\!=\!20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\!=\!20</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S5.T5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\!=\!40" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>40</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\!=\!40</annotation></semantics></math>
but saturates beyond <math id="S5.T5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\!=\!40" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>40</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\!=\!40</annotation></semantics></math> while latency increases linearly.
<math id="S5.T5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\!=\!40" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>40</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\!=\!40</annotation></semantics></math> was selected as the operating point.
</figcaption>
<table id="S5.T5.4" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S5.T5.4.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S5.T5.4.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><math id="S5.T5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<th id="S5.T5.4.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S5.T5.4.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Recall (Sem. Relevant)</span></th>
<th id="S5.T5.4.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S5.T5.4.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Avg. Latency</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S5.T5.4.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S5.T5.4.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">20</th>
<td id="S5.T5.4.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">95.8%</td>
<td id="S5.T5.4.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">301 ms</td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T5.4.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S5.T5.4.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row"><span id="S5.T5.4.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">40</span></th>
<td id="S5.T5.4.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="S5.T5.4.3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">99.34%</span></td>
<td id="S5.T5.4.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="S5.T5.4.3.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">436 ms</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T5.4.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S5.T5.4.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb">60</th>
<td id="S5.T5.4.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">99.5%</td>
<td id="S5.T5.4.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">611 ms</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Recall improved measurably from <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\!=\!20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\!=\!20</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\!=\!40" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>40</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\!=\!40</annotation></semantics></math> but
saturated beyond <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\!=\!40" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>40</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\!=\!40</annotation></semantics></math> while latency increased linearly.
We therefore selected <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\!=\!40" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>40</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\!=\!40</annotation></semantics></math> as the operating point balancing
coverage and computational cost.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Real-World Dataset (RWD).</h4>

<div id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To evaluate real-world behaviour we collected 1,247 consecutive live
queries from a real-world AI assistant deployment with full retrieval logs.
Each query carries a Business Query Detection (BQD) score in <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,100]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0,100</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,100]</annotation></semantics></math>
estimating whether knowledge-base retrieval is warranted
(score <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq\!50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq\!50</annotation></semantics></math>) or can be skipped (score <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;\!50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;\!50</annotation></semantics></math>).
This dataset captures the diversity of real-world production traffic
including navigational, compositional, and ambiguous queries.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Baselines.</h4>

<div id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Standard Top-K</span>: returns a fixed <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\!=\!10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\!=\!10</annotation></semantics></math> chunks regardless of
score distribution.
<span id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LLM Filter</span>: prompts <span id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">gpt-4o-mini</span> with a zero-shot
binary relevance judgement prompt that instructs the model to
distinguish topically-related but non-answering passages from
passages that directly address the query, without access to
<math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s_{i},r_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s_{i},r_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>. The full prompt and decoding configuration are
provided in Appendix <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B LLM Filter: Prompt and Decoding Configuration ‣ ScoreGate: Adaptive Chunk Selection forRetrieval-Augmented Generationvia Dual-Score Statistical Fusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsection">5.2  Bucket Distribution Analysis</h3>

<div id="S5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Before reporting precision and recall, we examine the empirical distribution of chunks across the four buckets on the ARB. Understanding bucket frequency is important because the B3 region (low similarity, high reranker score) is the key design feature of ScoreGate—it recovers semantically relevant chunks that bi-encoder retrieval ranks poorly due to vocabulary mismatch.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T6" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 6: </span>
<span id="S5.T6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Empirical bucket distribution on the ARB</span> (<math id="S5.T6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\!=\!300" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>300</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\!=\!300</annotation></semantics></math>).
B3 accounts for 18.7% of all candidates, confirming that
vocabulary-mismatch chunks are a substantial fraction of
production retrieval output.
</figcaption>
<table id="S5.T6.4" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S5.T6.4.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S5.T6.4.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S5.T6.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Bucket</span></th>
<th id="S5.T6.4.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S5.T6.4.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Condition</span></th>
<th id="S5.T6.4.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S5.T6.4.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Count</span></th>
<th id="S5.T6.4.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S5.T6.4.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">%</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S5.T6.4.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T6.4.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">B1 (keep always)</td>
<td id="S5.T6.4.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="S5.T6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}\geq\tau_{s}\wedge r_{i}\geq\tau_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>∧</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}\geq\tau_{s}\wedge r_{i}\geq\tau_{r}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S5.T6.4.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">134</td>
<td id="S5.T6.4.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">44.7%</td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T6.4.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T6.4.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">B2 (fuse, high bar)</td>
<td id="S5.T6.4.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.T6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}\geq\tau_{s}\wedge r_{i}&lt;\tau_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>∧</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}\geq\tau_{s}\wedge r_{i}&lt;\tau_{r}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S5.T6.4.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">55</td>
<td id="S5.T6.4.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">18.3%</td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T6.4.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T6.4.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">B3 (fuse, low bar)</td>
<td id="S5.T6.4.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.T6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}&lt;\tau_{s}\wedge r_{i}\geq\tau_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>∧</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}&lt;\tau_{s}\wedge r_{i}\geq\tau_{r}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S5.T6.4.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">56</td>
<td id="S5.T6.4.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">18.7%</td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T6.4.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T6.4.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">B4 (discard always)</td>
<td id="S5.T6.4.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="S5.T6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}&lt;\tau_{s}\wedge r_{i}&lt;\tau_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>∧</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}&lt;\tau_{s}\wedge r_{i}&lt;\tau_{r}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S5.T6.4.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">55</td>
<td id="S5.T6.4.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">18.3%</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The B3 region accounts for 56 of the 300 ARB candidates (18.7%). Of these 56 B3 chunks, 51 are in the Semantically Relevant category—confirming that B3 predominantly captures the vocabulary-mismatch pattern. The LLM Filter rejects 43 of these 56 B3 chunks (76.8%) due to low surface overlap, while ScoreGate retains 54 of 56 (96.4%) by trusting the cross-encoder signal. This single bucket accounts for the majority of the 6.93pp recall gap between ScoreGate and LLM Filter.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsection">5.3  Reranker-Only Baseline</h3>

<div id="S5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To isolate the contribution of dual-score fusion, we evaluated a
reranker-only baseline that retains chunk <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> iff
<math id="S5.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}\geq\tau_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}\geq\tau_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> without using embedding similarity <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T7" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 7: </span>
<span id="S5.T7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Reranker-only vs. ScoreGate on the ARB.</span>
Adding embedding similarity <math id="S5.T7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> via dual-score fusion improves
recall on both categories. Both methods observed zero false positives.
</figcaption>
<table id="S5.T7.4" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
