the knowledge base lacks relevant content, or the query is
non-retrieval in nature.</span></p></div></div>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_section" style="font-size:120%;">6  Discussion</h2>

<section id="S6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsection">6.1  Why Cross-Encoder Score Dominates in Fusion</h3>

<div id="S6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The 7:3 weighting of <math id="S6.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S6.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> in Equation <a href="#S4.E4" title="In 4.3 Weighted Fusion Score and Asymmetric Thresholds ‣ 4 ScoreGate Method ‣ ScoreGate: Adaptive Chunk Selection forRetrieval-Augmented Generationvia Dual-Score Statistical Fusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>
reflects training objective differences.
Bi-encoder similarity <math id="S6.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> comes from embeddings optimised for recall
at high-<math id="S6.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> rather than precision at low-<math id="S6.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>; the embedding space
represents topical relatedness rather than answer-level relevance.
The cross-encoder reranker is fine-tuned on query–document relevance
pairs with direct supervision, making <math id="S6.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> a stronger predictor of
context-inclusion appropriateness <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>, <a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsection">6.2  Ablation: Four-Bucket Structure vs. Single-Threshold Fusion</h3>

<div id="S6.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To verify that the four-bucket structure contributes beyond simply applying a single
threshold on the fusion score <math id="S6.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, we compare ScoreGate against a single-threshold
baseline: keep chunk <math id="S6.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="S6.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}\geq\theta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}\geq\theta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.
<math id="S6.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> was selected by grid search over <math id="S6.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0.10,0.40]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0.10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.40</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0.10,0.40]</annotation></semantics></math> in steps of 0.01,
maximising <math id="S6.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> on the same 200-query held-out validation set used to derive
<math id="S6.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{B2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{B2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S6.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{B3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{B3}</annotation></semantics></math> (disjoint from the ARB);
the optimal value was <math id="S6.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{*}\!=\!0.19" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>0.19</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{*}\!=\!0.19</annotation></semantics></math>.
On the ARB, ScoreGate achieves 99.34% recall on Semantically Relevant
chunks vs. 94.1% for the single-threshold baseline, and 97.77% vs. 93.2% on
Relevant chunks (zero observed false positives in both cases).
The gain arises because a single <math id="S6.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> cannot simultaneously
accommodate B2 (cross-encoder rejects, requiring a higher bar <math id="S6.SS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{B2}\!=\!0.255" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>0.255</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{B2}\!=\!0.255</annotation></semantics></math>)
and B3 (cross-encoder affirms, permitting a lower bar <math id="S6.SS2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{B3}\!=\!0.15" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>0.15</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{B3}\!=\!0.15</annotation></semantics></math>)—
the asymmetry is precisely what the four-bucket structure encodes.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsection">6.3  Failure Mode Analysis</h3>

<div id="S6.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">ScoreGate produces 3 false negatives on the ARB (2 Relevant, 1
Semantically Relevant missed chunks).
All three originate from the B2 or B3 borderline regions; none are
from high-confidence B4 rejection cases.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S6.T13" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 13: </span>
<span id="S6.T13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">ScoreGate false negatives on the ARB.</span>
All missed chunks involve semantic abstraction or indirect phrasing
that reduces both <math id="S6.T13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.T13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> below the fusion threshold.
</figcaption>
<table id="S6.T13.4" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
